ent, and material handling equipment; aerial work platforms, including boom and scissor lifts; and general tools and light equipment comprising pressure washers, water pumps, and power tools for construction and industrial companies, manufacturers, utilities, municipalities, homeowners, and government entities. The specialty segment rents trench safety equipment consists of trench shields, aluminum hydraulic shoring systems, slide rails, crossing plates, construction lasers, and line testing equipment for underground work; power and heating, ventilating, and air conditioning equipment, such as portable diesel generators, electrical distribution equipment, and temperature control equipment; fluid solutions equipment for fluid containment, transfer, and treatment; surface protection mats; and mobile storage equipment and modular office space. This segment serves construction companies involved in infrastructure projects, and municipalities and industrial companies. The company also sells aerial lifts, reach forklifts, telehandlers, compressors, and generators; construction consumables, tools, small equipment, and safety supplies; and parts for equipment that is owned by its customers, as well as provides repair and maintenance services. It sells used equipment through its sales force, brokers, website, at auctions, and directly to manufacturers. United Rentals, Inc. was incorporated in 1997 and is headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew J. Flannery | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28K people. Revenue per employee of $563K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["United Rentals, Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $65.4B market cap on $16.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 10% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","Accruals are elevated at -9.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 219% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.194137969703052},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $27.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-27328517.43},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"United Rentals, Inc. (NYSE:URI) Looks Like A Good Stock, And It's Going Ex-Dividend Soon","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-uri/united-rentals/news/united-rentals-inc-nyseuri-looks-like-a-good-stock-and-its-g","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793972002.189,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.915,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"United Rentals, Inc. $URI Shares Newly Bought by Mirae Asset Global Investments Co. Ltd.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/united-rentals-inc-uri-shares-newly-bought-by-mirae-asset-global-investments-co-ltd.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793790250.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.971,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"United Rentals' Specialty Revenue Surges 35%: What Comes Next?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/united-rentals-specialty-revenue-surges-180000416.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793815200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.821,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What United Rentals Doub